BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF A NIGHT AT THE DISCO BY CHRISTIAN JOHN W
 IKANE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T200000
UID:bm-5628020260702@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/ANightatt
 hedisco.jpg?cb=1780929710
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nFlying Books welcomes Christian John Wikane for
  the Toronto launch of his book A\nNIGHT AT THE DISCO.\nDJ Thomas del Pozo
  will lead Q&A.\n\nThis event is FREE and open to the public. Books will a
 lso be available for purchase at the event! Please\nRSVP\nto reserve your 
 seat.\nA Night at the Disco\nis a celebration of groundbreaking dance musi
 c from 1970–’79. An unprecedented collection of photographs of more th
 an 100 artists\, illuminating the styles and sounds from a decade that spa
 rked a global phenomenon in music and culture. Exclusive comments from Don
 na Summer\, Barry Gibb\, Debbie Harry\, Giorgio Moroder\, founding members
  of CHIC\, Labelle\, The Trammps\, Village People\, Earth\, Wind & Fire\, 
 and dozens more artists\, songwriters and producers\, offering fascinating
  insights that tell the stories behind the beats. From underground New Yor
 k clubs to discothèques across the globe\n\, A Night at the Disco\nillust
 rates how artists spanning soul\, pop\, disco\, funk\, jazz and rock defin
 ed nightlife during the 1970s and influenced popular music to the present 
 day. With a foreword by Verdine White of Earth\, Wind & Fire\, this is a r
 eal treat for music\, dance and disco fans everywhere.\nChristian John Wik
 ane is a NYC-based music journalist and essayist who has interviewed more 
 than 600 recording artists over two decades\, including Paul McCartney\, J
 anelle Monáe\, Donna Summer\, Annie Lennox\, and Carly Simon. He is a con
 tributing writer for PEOPLE Magazine and served as Contributing Editor for
  PopMatters from 2006–2023. He has been credited as a consultant on HBO'
 s Emmy-nominated\nTina\n(2021)\, CNN's D\nionne Warwick: Don't Make Me Ove
 r\n(2021)\, and HBO's\nLove to Love You\, Donna Summer (\n2022). A sought-
 after moderator\, he has curated and led events at the Apollo Theater\, Br
 ooklyn Museum\, Lincoln Center\, and Joe's Pub. He is the author of Casabl
 anca Records:\nPlay It Again\n(2009) and co-author of\nWhat the Band Wore:
  Fashion & Music\n(2023) — a\nWall Street Journal T\nop 20 Pick — and\
 nA Night at the Disco\n(2026).\nThomas del Pozo is a Toronto-based vinyl D
 J\, record collector and long-time disco aficionado and historian. Thomas 
 has been writing about disco music for over 20 years\, beginning with his 
 blog\nDisco Delivery\nand has authored liner notes for disco reissues on v
 arious independent labels. Thomas is passionate about the history of disco
 \, its place in LGBTQ liberation and its continuing relevance across audie
 nces and age groups.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
